# LOOM-8 on the SMK-37 (smk37.c): the pads are the FM-1's 16 white keys. On Steps a tap writes the remembered notes
# on the step (again: clears it); the pads' lights follow the steps (padleds: the ink, mid for a step with notes)
wait 300
turn ALGO 1
wait 30
expect trk 2
expect page Steps
pad 0 down 100
wait 30
pad 0 up
wait 60
expect note 2 1 1 60
pad 3 down 100
wait 30
pad 3 up
wait 60
expect note 2 1 4 60
padleds
shot pads.png
pad 0 down 100
wait 30
pad 0 up
wait 60
expect note 2 1 1 0
# the pads play where the white keys play: Mix (GLO), velocity from the pad
tap GLO
wait 30
expect page Mix
pad 2 down 90
wait 60
expect voices 1
pad 2 up
wait 150
expect voices 0
# SAVE held + pad 2: the project to slot 2
tap SEQ
wait 30
press SAVE
wait 30
pad 1 down 100
wait 30
pad 1 up
wait 30
release SAVE
wait 150
expect dirty 0
